# >>> carbon (generated + derived — safe to keep, rebuildable) >>>
# generated tool dirs (materialized copies — stamped, never hand-edited)
.claude/
.cursor/
.opencode/
CLAUDE.md
# generated truth + transient meld state
**/.carbon/lock.json
**/.carbon/.resolved-set.json
**/.carbon/.resolved-set.json.run.*
**/.carbon/store/
**/.carbon/.lock
# derived skill-memory (catalog, BM25 index, knowledge graph, HTML report)
**/.carbon/catalog.json
**/.carbon/index/
**/.carbon/graph/
**/.carbon/graph.json
**/.carbon/report.html
**/.carbon/graph.html
# canonical layout: all derived machinery (store, lock, index, graph) lives here
**/.carbon/derived/
# cortex run state (frozen plans + journals — regenerable, per-run). Receipts
# are NOT ignored: they are durable proof and belong in the repo.
**/.carbon/cortex/
# opt-in local telemetry (never committed)
**/.carbon/telemetry.jsonl
# exported libraries (rebuildable via `carbon export`; publish from their own repo)
**/.carbon/export/
# signing PRIVATE keys — never commit (the public key + carbon.sig.json ARE committed)
carbon.key
**/carbon.key
# <<< carbon <<<

# inbound dependency checkouts — fetched from `sources:` pins, never committed.
# Kept OUTSIDE the carbon block above: spine regenerates that block on every install.
**/.carbon/sources/
**/.carbon/self/submodules/
